guamp: "nobocache" in the board's NativeTurnipDebug sets TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE=0 (AdrenoMetal 2ff4be9 plugin)

The newer Turnip Darwin backend (UniXNU feat/ipados27-gpu-parity c7353ea7..2c40ae9, guamp UniXNU branch guamp/turnip-ipados27-20261029)
keeps freed BOs in a size-class cache, given back on OOM retry and memory pressure only; guamp's kernel never reports
NativeAdrenoParamsPoolPressure. The board switch turns the cache off without a new Turnip: GuampAdrenoProbe.cpp NativeTurnipDebug
"nocb,noconform,sysmem,nobocache" (kernel build). Without the word nothing changes.

diff --git a/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm b/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
index 9a4f183..e03de5b 100644
--- a/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
+++ b/NativeAdrenoMetalPlugin.mm
@@ -262,8 +262,14 @@ static void applyBoardTurnipDebug(unsigned port) {
     CFTypeRef value = copyProperty ? copyProperty(port, CFSTR("NativeTurnipDebug"), kCFAllocatorDefault, 0) : nullptr;
     if (!value) return;
     char text[128];
-    if (CFGetTypeID(value) == CFStringGetTypeID() && CFStringGetCString((CFStringRef) value, text, sizeof text, kCFStringEncodingUTF8))
+    if (CFGetTypeID(value) == CFStringGetTypeID() && CFStringGetCString((CFStringRef) value, text, sizeof text, kCFStringEncodingUTF8)) {
         setenv("TU_DEBUG", text, 1);
+        // guamp (UniXNU-guamp patches/adreno-metal/0005): "nobocache" in the board's NativeTurnipDebug turns off the BO cache of the
+        // newer Turnip Darwin backend (UniXNU c7353ea7 and later, TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE=0): every free goes back to the kernel at once,
+        // as with the older backend, should cached BOs crowd the gpu-all windows or the BO limit of all processes. TU_DEBUG ignores
+        // the unknown word; an older Turnip ignores the variable.
+        if (strstr(text, "nobocache")) setenv("TU_DARWIN_BO_CACHE", "0", 1);
+    }
     CFRelease(value);
 }
 static id deviceForPort(unsigned port) {
